<article class="env-remark" id="0BVP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BVP">Remark <span data-tag="0BVP">49.6.4</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a quasi-finite homomorphism of Noetherian rings. Let $J$ be the annihilator of $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(B \otimes _ A B \to B)$. There is a canonical $B$-bilinear pairing </p>
  <div class="equation" id="0BVQ">
    <span class="equation-label"><a href="/tag/0BVQ" data-tag="0BVQ">49.6.4.1</a></span>
  <div>\begin{equation}  \label{discriminant-equation-pairing-noether} \omega _{B/A} \times J \longrightarrow B \end{equation}</div>
</div>
  <p> defined as follows. Choose a factorization $A \to B' \to B$ with $A \to B'$ finite and $B' \to B$ inducing an open immersion of spectra. Let $J'$ be the annihilator of $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(B' \otimes _ A B' \to B')$. We first define </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(B', A) \times J' \longrightarrow B',\quad (\lambda , \sum b_ i \otimes c_ i) \longmapsto \sum \lambda (b_ i)c_ i  \]
</div>
  <p> This is $B'$-bilinear exactly because for $\xi \in J'$ and $b \in B'$ we have $(b \otimes 1)\xi = (1 \otimes b)\xi $. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0BVN" data-tag="0BVN">49.6.3</a> and the fact that $\omega _{B/A} = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(B', A) \otimes _{B'} B$ we can extend this to a $B$-bilinear pairing as displayed above. </p>
</article>